{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an image-only model using ResNet50 encoder, achieving validation accuracy of 0.2079 and F1 of 0.1718, significantly lower than RNA-only baselines (e.g., 0.4849–0.6501). The results suggest image modality may not contribute meaningfully to performance in this configuration, but the impact of specific image encoder choices or fusion methods remains uncertain without direct comparison. Multimodal approaches combining RNA and image data were not evaluated."
}

